

**15.3.24**: \(F(a,\,b;a+b-\frac{1}{2};\,a)\)\(=\)\((1-z)^{-\sharp}F(2a-1,2b-1;a+b-\frac{1}{2};\frac{1}{2}-\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{1-z})\)
**15.3.25**: \(=\)\((1-z)^{-\sharp}\)\((\frac{1}{2}+\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{1-z})^{1-2a}\)\(F\)\(\left(2a-1,\,a-b+1;\,a+b-\frac{1}{2};\frac{\sqrt{1-z}-1}{\sqrt{1-z}+1}\right)\)
**15.3.26**: \(F(a,\,b;\,a-b+1;\,z)\)\(=\)\((1+z)^{-\sharp}F\)\((\frac{1}{2}a,\,\frac{1}{2}a+\frac{1}{2};\,a-b+1;\,4z(1+z)^{-\sharp})\)
**15.3.27**: \(=\)\((1\pm\sqrt{z})^{-2a}F(a,\,a-b+\frac{1}{2};\,2a-2b+1;\,\pm 4\sqrt{z}(1\pm\sqrt{z})^{- 2})\)
**15.3.28**: \(=\)\((1-z)^{-\sharp}F(\frac{1}{2}a,\,\frac{1}{2}a-b+1;-4z(1-z)^{-\sharp})\)
**15.3.29**: \(F\left(a,\,b;\,\frac{1}{2}a+\frac{1}{2}b+\frac{1}{2};\,z\right)\)\(=\)\((1-2z)^{-\sharp}F\)\(\left(\frac{1}{2}a,\,\frac{1}{2}a+\frac{1}{2};\,\frac{1}{2}a-\frac{1}{2}z \right)\)
**15.3.30**: \(=\)\(F(\frac{1}{2}a,\,\frac{1}{2}b;\,\frac{1}{2}a+\frac{1}{2}b+\frac{1}{2};\,4z^{ -\sharp})\)
**15.3.31**: \(F(a,\,1-a;\,e;\,z)\)\(=\)\((1-z)^{-\sharp}F(\frac{1}{2}c-\frac{1}{2}a,\,\frac{1}{2}c+\frac{1}{2}a-\frac{1}{2};\,c;\,4z- 4z^{\sharp})\)
**15.3.32**: \(=\)\((1-z)^{\varepsilon-1}(1-2z)^{\varepsilon-\varepsilon}F\)\((\frac{1}{2}c-\frac{1}{2}a,\,\frac{1}{2}c-\frac{1}{2}a+\frac{1}{2};\,e;\,(4z^{ 2}-4z)(1-2z)^{-\sharp})\)

**Public transformations are listed in [15.2] and [15.3].**

**In the formulas above, the square roots are defined so that their value is real and positive when \(0\leq z<1\). All formulas are valid in the neighborhood of \(z=0\).**

**15.4. Special Cases of \(F(a,\,b;\,e;\,z)\)**

**Polynomials**

When \(a\) or \(b\) is equal to a negative integer, then

**15.4.1**: \(F(-m,\,b;\,e;\,z)\)\(=\)\(\sum\limits_{n=0}^{m}\frac{(-m)_{n}(b)_{n}}{(c)_{n}}\frac{z^{n}}{n!}\)

